# WLLPR — Free Unlimited 4K Wallpapers

**Generate stunning abstract landscape wallpapers in 4K. Free, unlimited, no AI, no tokens, no sign-up.**

WLLPR draws every wallpaper from scratch with code — no image files, no models, no API calls. Pick a pattern, tweak the colors, and export a crisp PNG for your desktop or phone. As many as you want, forever.

👉 **[Browse presets](https://bypedroneres.github.io/wallpaper-generator/index.html)** — start from ~168 ready-made wallpapers
👉 **[Create your own](https://bypedroneres.github.io/wallpaper-generator/create/index.html)** — the live editor

---

## Why WLLPR

- **Truly free & unlimited** — no paywall, no credits, no rate limits. Generate a thousand wallpapers if you like.
- **No AI, no tokens** — nothing is generated by a model or billed per image. Every scene is pure procedural graphics running in your browser.
- **4K ready** — export at full desktop resolution (3840 × 2160) or iPhone (1290 × 2796).
- **Instant & private** — everything renders locally on an HTML5 canvas. No uploads, no accounts, no tracking.
- **Weightless** — wallpapers are stored as tiny "recipes" (a few parameters), not heavy image files, so the whole gallery loads instantly.

## What you can make

Six procedurally-generated scene types:

- 🌲 **Flowing hills** with scattered pine trees
- 🌊 **Smooth waves**
- 🏜️ **Sand dunes**
- ⛰️ **Jagged mountains**
- ◎ **Concentric arcs**
- 〰️ **Free-form desert scribbles**

Each scene can be:

- Recolored across **13 hand-tuned palettes**
- Flipped between **light and dark** variants
- Previewed with a live **macOS-style clock overlay**
- Exported as a high-resolution **PNG** (desktop 4K or iPhone)

## How to use it

1. **Start from a preset** → open the [home page](https://bypedroneres.github.io/wallpaper-generator/index.html) and browse the carousels by pattern type.
2. **Or build your own** → open the [editor](https://bypedroneres.github.io/wallpaper-generator/create/index.html), pick a pattern, choose a palette, toggle light/dark, and hit **Generate variation** to roll a fresh random seed.
3. **Download** → grab it as **Desktop 4K** (3840 × 2160) or **iPhone** (1290 × 2796).

That's it. No login, no export limit.

## How it works

Every wallpaper is generated by a single deterministic engine, so the same **seed** always reproduces the exact same image.

- **`js/engine.js`** — the core. A `mulberry32` seeded random-number generator, 1-D value noise smoothed with fbm (fractional Brownian motion) for natural ridgelines, and a `lerpColor` helper for smooth gradients. Six draw functions (`drawFlowingHills`, `drawSmoothWave`, `drawSandDunes`, `drawMountains`, `drawConcentricArcs`, `drawDesertDunes`) layer translucent shapes for depth. `drawClockOverlay` renders the date/time; `exportWallpaper` re-renders at full resolution to an off-screen canvas and saves a PNG.
- **`js/wallpapers.js`** — the data layer. ~168 wallpaper "recipes," each just `{ pattern, palette, seed, mode, id, name }`. Because rendering is deterministic, these tiny objects reproduce every wallpaper on demand at any resolution.
- **`js/home.js`** — renders thumbnails, the featured hero, and one scrollable carousel per pattern section.
- **`js/detail.js`** — full-screen view; reads the wallpaper id from the URL, redraws at full size, and offers a download dropdown.
- **`js/create.js`** — the editor; builds the pattern grid and palette swatches, handles the light/dark toggle and shuffle, and re-renders desktop + mobile previews live.

### Design decisions

- **Recipes, not files** — storing 168 full-res PNGs would bloat the repo. Since generation is deterministic, saving only the four parameters that define each image lets the browser regenerate anything instantly, from a 320px thumbnail to a 4K export.
- **Vanilla JS, no framework** — ES modules and direct DOM manipulation are clearer than adding a build step for a project this size. It deploys to GitHub Pages with no compilation (a `.nojekyll` file ensures the `js/` folder is served correctly).

## Tech

Vanilla JavaScript (ES modules), HTML5 Canvas, and CSS. No front-end framework, no build step. Deployed as a static site on GitHub Pages. A light/dark theme choice is persisted in `localStorage`.

> A companion desktop build (Tauri) on a separate branch can set the wallpaper directly on macOS. This web version is the primary, self-contained release.

## Run locally

Because it uses ES modules, serve it over HTTP rather than opening the file directly:

```bash
# from the project root
python3 -m http.server 8000
# then open http://localhost:8000
